# sapintegrationsuite_integration_assessment_technology_style (Resource)

A technology style entry says that a technology supports an integration style of SAP's
Integration Solution Advisory Methodology, for example process or data integration. The
assessment uses a technology's styles, together with its domains and key characteristic ratings,
when it recommends technologies for an interface.

**Status:** supported. SAP's Entities API specification on the Business Accelerator Hub
documents this entity, and its requests were verified on a tenant. No opt-in switch is needed.
Every change replaces the entry, so unlike the links of the landscape objects nothing here
needs `enable_unofficial = true`.

## Prerequisites

- The `integration_assessment` provider block, with the service key of an
  *Integration Assessment APIs* service instance (plan `default`). The Cloud Integration
  credentials do not work for this API.
- An Integration Assessment subscription in the subaccount.
- The technology's Id, from [`sapintegrationsuite_integration_assessment_technology`](integration_assessment_technology.md) (resource or data source), and the style's Id from the [`sapintegrationsuite_integration_assessment_style`](../data-sources/integration_assessment_style.md) data source.

## Ids

The taxonomy entries (domains, styles, key characteristic values, recommendation degrees) are
SAP's reference content, but their Ids are assigned per tenant. Never write them into a
configuration: look them up by name with the data sources, as in the example below.

## Lifecycle

| Operation | What happens |
|---|---|
| Create | Links the technology to the style. |
| Read | Reads both links. |
| Update | None: the service has no update for this entity. |
| Replacement | Any change deletes the entry and creates a new one. |
| Delete | Deletes the entry. The technology and the taxonomy entries stay. |

